course: dictionary
lesson: 4071
title: What is geology?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Geology is the science of the Earth. It studies rocks, soil, minerals, volcanoes and earthquakes, and how the Earth has changed over time. A scientist who studies geology is a geologist. Look at the context: «People have always built with local stone, so old towns often show the local geology.» The clues are stone and old towns, so geology must be about the rocks under the ground.
explain: Geology has a second meaning too: the rocks and land of one particular place. «The geology of Scotland» means the rocks and land features found in Scotland. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The rocks and land of Scotland» still makes sense, so you have understood it.
explain: The second example sentence is harder: «When plates collide, layers of rock can be bent into folds like a rug pushed against a wall.» The comparison to a rug helps you picture it. Rock layers can bend like cloth when the Earth's plates push together. Comparisons are useful context clues.
fact: Geology is the science of the Earth's rocks, soil, minerals, volcanoes and earthquakes.
fact: A geologist is a scientist who studies geology.
fact: Rocks come in three main kinds: igneous, sedimentary and metamorphic.
fact: «The honey-coloured limestone of Bath» is an example of local geology, because the stone comes from the land around the city.
fact: Geologists help people find water, oil and safe ground for buildings.
exercise: «Geology» means which of these? | The study of plants and animals | The study of stars and planets | The making of old castles | *The science of the Earth's rocks and how it has changed
exercise: «Igneous», «sedimentary» and «metamorphic» are all kinds of what? | Clouds | Plants | *Rock | Sounds
exercise: Which person studies geology? | A teacher of music | A pilot who flies planes | A baker who makes bread | *A geologist
test: «When plates collide, layers of rock can be bent into folds like a rug pushed against a wall.» What does this sentence show? | Rugs are made from rock | Walls are stronger than rock | Plates are shaped like rugs | *Rock layers can bend when the Earth's plates push together
test: Why do old towns often show the local geology? | *Because they were built from stone found nearby | Because people painted their walls with rock | Because geology is a type of rug | Because they are always near the sea
exam: A geologist would most likely study which of these? | A sunny beach holiday | A recipe for chocolate cake | A new pair of football boots | *A volcano and the rocks around it
